Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.3.0-0

%labels
    Maintainer sdweave2@ncsu.edu
    Source https://bitbucket.org/MAVERICLab/vcontact3
    Version 3.1.6

%help
    vConTACT3 — Viral Contig Automatic Clustering and Taxonomy.
    Clusters viral genomes with a reference database and assigns
    taxonomy from shared protein clusters.

    Usage:
        apptainer run vcontact3-3.1.6.sif <subcommand> [options]

    Subcommands (see `vcontact3 --help` for the full list and flags):
        run       - Cluster user genomes with the reference database
        prepare_databases - Download/prepare a reference database
        version   - Print the installed version

    Example:
        apptainer run vcontact3-3.1.6.sif run --nucleotide genomes.fna \
            --db-path /path/to/vcontact3_db --output vcontact3_out -t 8
        apptainer run vcontact3-3.1.6.sif --help

    Note: built in-house instead of using the quay.io biocontainer.
    vcontact3 3.1.6 only requires pandas>=2.1.1 with no upper bound,
    and the pyhdfd78af_1 biocontainer resolved pandas 3.0.3. pandas 3
    raises on profiles.py:377 (assigning a string into a float64
    column), so this image pins the data stack to pandas-2-era
    versions.

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # Hazel bind-mount points
    mkdir -p /rs1 /share /home /usr/local/usrapps

    # Install vcontact3 via bioconda using mamba (see CLAUDE.md lesson 2).
    # The recipe leaves pandas (and most of the data stack) unbounded, so a
    # fresh solve drifts onto pandas 3, which breaks
    # profiles.py:377 with "TypeError: Invalid value 'withUser' for dtype
    # 'float64'". Pin vcontact3's direct dependencies to the versions in the
    # quay.io pyhdfd78af_0 biocontainer, built while 3.1.6 was current
    # (same failure class as CLAUDE.md lesson 9). No GPU-capable
    # dependencies, so no GPU addendum applies.
    mamba create -n vcontact3 -y -c conda-forge -c bioconda \
        vcontact3=3.1.6 \
        "python=3.11" \
        "pandas=2.3.3" \
        "numpy=1.26.4" \
        "scipy=1.16.2" \
        "scikit-learn=1.7.2" \
        "scikit-bio=0.7.0" \
        "pyarrow=21.0.0" \
        "pytables=3.10.2" \
        "matplotlib-base=3.10.7"
    mamba clean -afy

%environment
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export PATH="/opt/conda/envs/vcontact3/bin:$PATH"

%runscript
    exec vcontact3 "$@"

%test
    . /opt/conda/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
    conda activate vcontact3
    vcontact3 --help
    # Guard against the pandas 3 regression this image exists to avoid.
    python -c "import pandas, sys; v = pandas.__version__; print('pandas', v); sys.exit(0 if v.startswith('2.') else 1)"
